Fix the dip switch context address of Rambo

The context address of Rambo (SBQL) was the address of the game's amDipswInit
itself, so the detoured amDipswInit wrote into the game's read-only code. The
segfault handler then skipped the faulting bytes one by one and the game ran
whatever was left, which crashes it depending on the build. Use the context
variable the game's own amDipsw functions read.

--- a/src/loader/patching/patch.c
+++ b/src/loader/patching/patch.c
@@ -2606,7 +2606,7 @@
             // patchMemoryFromString(0x080e3f79, "01");
             patchMemoryFromString(0x080e3e2e, "EB");
             // Fixes
-            amDipswContextAddr = (void *)0x082c2f94;
+            amDipswContextAddr = (void *)0x0acad988;
             detourFunction(0x082c2f94, amDipswInit);
             detourFunction(0x082c3018, amDipswExit);
             detourFunction(0x082c308d, amDipswGetData);
